  {#- ---- 3. THE SCOREBOARD ---- -#}
  <section class="cs-about__section">
    {#- ss10, THE O TARGET, AND THE ONE PLACE ON THIS PAGE IT IS LEGAL.

        DESIGN_SYSTEM.md retires the O device in any headline sharing a visual
        field with the isotype, and permits it where the icon is not present.
        Measured rather than assumed: at 1440 by 900 the isotype sits at y 28
        and the h1 at y 339, both inside one viewport, so the h1 is retired
        ground however much its A-B-O-U-T would like the glyph. This heading is
        roughly three thousand pixels down, with the masthead long gone.

        THE SWAP IS JUSTIFIED BY MEANING, which is the bar the heading macro's
        own note sets and which who-we-are enforced by dropping a swap that was
        available rather than meaningful. A target device on the O of Scoreboard
        is the closest meaning match anywhere on this site: the glyph is a
        scoring mark and the word is the score.

        ONE SWAP, NOT TWO. Scoreboard carries two Os and the cap is two, so the
        build would allow both. Both is the thing the rules exist to prevent:
        the device stops reading as a decision at volume.

        THE HEADING GOES THROUGH THE MACRO rather than being hand-written like
        the one above it, because the macro is the enforcement path. glyphSwaps
        checks the cap, checks the tag is h1 or h2, and checks the letter falls
        inside the named word, and it warns and renders plain rather than
        failing silently.

        THE WORD CHANGED FROM "Measured" TO "Scoreboard", and that is a copy
        edit I am flagging rather than burying. Scoreboard is the brief's own
        word for this section. It is also what gave the device a legal home,
        which is the wrong reason to rename a heading, so it is only defensible
        because the first reason stands on its own. Reverse it and the glyph
        goes with it. -#}
    {{ heading("Scoreboard", as="h2", class="cs-about__h2",
               swaps={ word: "Scoreboard", letter: "o", flavor: "alt-dot" }) }}
